The Daily Program Presents: Forecast Loops

Launching on Tuesday, July 28th



Video no longer means the same thing to everyone. Wealth, infrastructure, age, language, and power shape who gets to make and circulate images, who becomes visible through them, and whose histories get recognized by the systems that generate and distribute them. For some, this environment means swimming in a constant stream of high-speed, synthetic media. For others, it's encountered through surveillance, gig labor, targeted ads, or images imported from elsewhere.



Contemporary video doesn't sit on one shared timeline. It moves as several unequal presents unfolding alongside each other.



We're proud to present Forecast Loops, a new group show that treats this unevenness as its starting point. The show brings together 13 artists working across different approaches to the moving image:

